> I've read the guidebook, but still have some questions:
>
> (a) Is there a way to see your own intrinsics?  I'm referring to, for
> example, the abilities a monk gets as he progresses levels (stealth,
> warning, etc.)  You get it when you die, but I can't find a way to
> display it in the game (seems like "Player's Handbook" material to me).
>  Or is there some magic item or tool that reveals this?

Wand of enlightment is the most reliable.

The big thing is to track all of the messages.  When
you gain an intrinsic there is an associated message.
Filtering through all of those "You kill the orcish
wizard" messages make it tempting to blow past them,
but miss "You feel full of hot air" and you've missed
noticing that you just acquired an intrinsic.  Same
with "You kill the next.  Welcome to level 14.  You
feel more confident in your skills.  You feel in
control of yourself."  If all you notice is the
gained level, you've missed some crucial stuff.

For the ones gained by character types at certan
levels, that's in the spoilers.  I start at
www.nethack.org, say friend to enter, follow the links
link, and I go to one of the spoiler sites.  I
generally used Kate N's.  Just in case I have the
sources unwrapped on a UNIX box somewhere.

> (b) How do you tunnel through walls?  Do you need a tool to do that?

There are two common weapon/tools that can do it,
plus a wand, a spell and probably other ways.

In Nethack walls range from normal diggability
through tough to dig through to undigable.  If
at first you don't suceed, learn what the message
means so you know whether trying again will waste
your time.  ;^)

> (c) On a related note...I take it you can push boulders but not pull
> them...correct?

Not completely correct.  A character with no items
at all carried can sometimes squeeze through.  (A
rediculously strong character might end up picking
it up; good luck picking up so much as a gem until
you drop the boulder).  And get killed by the hoard
of hungry nasties on the other side of course ...

> Periodically I'll be going down a hallway and come to
> a boulder...sometimes I can't push it or there's a monster on the other
> side.  Is it possible to get stuck in the game (i.e., no down
> staircase) because of a boulder?

There are various ways to get around that.  Boulders
are not indestructable.  Walls near boulders are
usually not indestructable.  There's even the stone
to flesh spell.  Given the right situation, who needs
to turn that delicious boulder into meat ...

Note that at times boulders are a valuable limited
resource.  Don't push them against the outer walls
until you know this isn't such a level.

> (d) Is it just my luck or do Monks start with and find a ton of food?
> All of my Cavemen so far have had to pray, but a couple of my Monks
> started with a veritable smorgasboard and were finding food rations
> left and right.  Is that game balance because Monks are vegetarians?

I think it is game balance.  Note that vegitarian
conduct is a challenge not mandatory.  Finding food
is definitely just your (real world not game counter)
luck.

> (e) Is there a way to say "rest until healed" or do you just have to
> keep hitting '.'?  I've found just holding it down is too dangerous ;)

I tend to move back up a level or two and cruise
for some weaker monsters that might leave me
something in their wills.

If you can estimate how long you'll need to wait,
you can try "100s".  It will search (more beneficial
than pure rest) for that many turns unless interupted.

